Here is an optimized ExtendScript (`.jsx`) for Adobe InDesign. 

When InDesign nativey turns off "Facing Pages", it often shifts layouts or recalculates margins (turning Inside/Outside into Left/Right incorrectly based on the page side). 

This script safely disables layout adjustment algorithms, records the exact absolute margins of every single page (including masters), switches the document to single pages, and then reapplies those exact margins to prevent text frames and elements from shifting.

### How to use:
1. Save the code below in a plain text file and name it `ConvertToSinglePages.jsx`.
2. Place it in your InDesign Scripts Panel folder (or run it via `File > Scripts > Run Script`).
3. Open your facing-pages document and run the script.

```javascript
//@target indesign

function main() {
    if (app.documents.length === 0) {
        alert("Please open a document first.");
        return;
    }

    var doc = app.activeDocument;

    if (!doc.documentPreferences.facingPages) {
        alert("Document is already set to single pages.");
        return;
    }

    // Wrap in doScript for a single Undo step and faster script execution
    app.doScript(
        function() { processDocument(doc); }, 
        ScriptLanguage.JAVASCRIPT, 
        [], 
        UndoModes.ENTIRE_SCRIPT, 
        "Convert to Single Pages"
    );
}

function processDocument(doc) {
    // 1. Disable layout adjustments to strictly prevent elements from shifting
    doc.layoutAdjustmentPreferences.enableLayoutAdjustment = false;

    // Check for newer CC "Adjust Layout" feature and disable it
    if (doc.hasOwnProperty('adjustLayoutPreferences')) {
        doc.adjustLayoutPreferences.enableAdjustLayout = false;
    }

    // 2. Set ruler origin to PAGE to ensure coordinate safety regardless of spread width
    var originalRulerOrigin = doc.viewPreferences.rulerOrigin;
    doc.viewPreferences.rulerOrigin = RulerOrigin.PAGE_ORIGIN;

    // 3. Store the precise absolute margins for all document pages and master pages
    // Reading Left/Right here translates Inside/Outside based on current page side before we change it.
    var docPageData = storeMargins(doc.pages);
    var masterPageData = storeMargins(doc.masterSpreads.everyItem().pages.everyItem().getElements());

    // 4. Change document to single pages
    doc.documentPreferences.facingPages = false;

    // 5. Restore the exact margins to all pages (now applied strictly as Left/Right)
    restoreMargins(docPageData);
    restoreMargins(masterPageData);

    // 6. Restore original ruler settings
    doc.viewPreferences.rulerOrigin = originalRulerOrigin;

    alert("Success! Document converted to single pages.");
}

function storeMargins(pages) {
    var data = [];
    for (var i = 0; i < pages.length; i++) {
        var p = pages[i];
        var m = p.marginPreferences;

        data.push({
            page: p,
            top: m.top,
            bottom: m.bottom,
            left: m.left,  // Records the absolute left (Inside for right pages, Outside for left pages)
            right: m.right // Records the absolute right
        });
    }
    return data;
}

function restoreMargins(data) {
    for (var i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {
        var item = data[i];
        if (item.page.isValid) {
            var m = item.page.marginPreferences;
            m.top = item.top;
            m.bottom = item.bottom;
            m.left = item.left;
            m.right = item.right;
        }
    }
}

// Run script
main();
```

### What this script does:
1. **Disables Auto-Adjust:** Turns off "Layout Adjustment" and "Adjust Layout" (CC) so InDesign doesn't try to automatically resize or move your artwork when the page boundaries change.
2. **Standardizes Coordinates:** Changes the ruler origin to `Page Origin`, meaning elements remember where they are relative to their specific page, rather than the spread spine.
3. **Array Caching:** Caches the Left, Right, Top, and Bottom margins of every document and master page.
4. **Turns off Facing Pages.**
5. **Restores Margins:** Applies the cached margins back so your margins don't invert or expand unexpectedly.

